# ---- INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION ----
# The script reporting its own PASS is not evidence that tokens moved. Horizon
# confirms both permitted transactions, and the SAC balances reconcile exactly:
# only the two permitted supplies landed, and the denied one moved nothing.
#
#   pool          21000000  = 20000000 (control) + 1000000 (capped, under cap)
#   smart account 60000000  = 81000000 funded - 21000000 moved
#
# The pool balance is also what proves the nested `transfer` leg executed at all,
# rather than the pool merely accepting a `submit` and moving nothing.

$ curl -s https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org/transactions/ccbab9835d7f…
successful= True ledger= 4434552
$ curl -s https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org/transactions/e7092ed99735…
successful= True ledger= 4434553
$ SAC balance(pool) / balance(smart account)
pool            21000000
smart account   60000000

# ---- MUTATION: does the deny track the CAP VALUE, or merely the presence of a
# ---- second policy on the rule? Raise the cap to 50000000 so the same
# ---- 20000000 supply now sits UNDER it. Everything else is identical.
# ---- The verdict flips, so the cap value is what refused. Script exits 1.

$ sed 's/CAP_STROOPS = 5_000_000n/CAP_STROOPS = 50_000_000n/' && bun … --network testnet
